Project Spark
===========


Start off by following these steps:
----------------------


Create the directories
----------------------

As a first step, you'll have to create and enter a folder with the appropriate name.
To do that, run these commands:

```bash
   mkdir spark
   cd spark
```

To initialize your local repository, run this command:
------------------------------------------------------

```bash
   repo init -u https://github.com/Spark-OPPO/manifest -b pyro-next --git-lfs
```

Afterwards, sync the source by running this command:
----------------

```bash
repo sync --force-sync --optimized-fetch --no-tags --no-clone-bundle --prune -j$(nproc --all)
```


Building Spark
---------------

In case you are building Mac OS X, you are required to install coreutils from MacPorts before you continue.
In order to build, use this command:
```bash
   . build/env*
   lunch spark_<devicecodename>-userdebug
   mka bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

### Build SparkOS for OPPO R9sPlus
```bash
rm -rf device/qcom/sepolicy hardware/qcom-caf/msm8953/audio hardware/qcom-caf/msm8953/display hardware/qcom-caf/msm8953/media
git clone https://github.com/Spark-OPPO/android_device_qcom_sepolicy -b pyro-next device/qcom/sepolicy
git clone https://github.com/Spark-OPPO/android_hardware_qcom_audio -b pyro-next hardware/qcom-caf/msm8953/audio
git clone https://github.com/Spark-OPPO/android_hardware_qcom_display -b pyro-next hardware/qcom-caf/msm8953/display
git clone https://github.com/Spark-OPPO/android_hardware_qcom_media -b pyro-next hardware/qcom-caf/msm8953/media
```

After building:
---------------

Be sure to check our [**documents repo**](https://github.com/Spark-Rom/Stuff) for any queries.
